->1

-int(False)
->0

8.Arithmetic & Assignment Operators
num1=3
num2=5

*Arithmetic operators
# + -> Addition operator
-num1+num2

# - ->Substraction operator
num1-num2

# * ->Multiplication operator
num1*num2

# / ->Division operator
num1/num2 *result will be in float

# // -> Floor division
num1//num2 *result will be in int

# % ->modulus
num1%num2

# **  ->exponent or power
5 ** 2

#Assignment Operators
value=100,= is assignment operator

#compund operator
x=10
x +=1 # x = x + 1

x -=1 # x = x - 1

9.Comparison & logical operator
#comparision operator
# ==,!=,>,<,>=,<=
num1=10
num2=20
num3=10
*num1==num3

*num1!=20

*num2>=num1

*num1<=num3

#Logical operators
#and,or,not

*true and true
-true
*true and false
-false
* in and operator both condition should be true

*true or true
-true
*true or false
-true
*false or false
-false
*in or operator at least one should be true

*not true
-false
*not false
-true

10. Associativity & Precedence of operators
#presidence
12+33*10
-340(bodmas rule) also when division comes priority start from left to right

name="Mark"
age=22

name=="Mark" or name=="John" and age<18
-True (cause first priority is and)

f=(name=="Mark" or name=="John") and age<18
-False #bracket has highest priority than and ,or

2**1**3
=2(in exponent associativity is from right to left)

11.Printing to console - the print() function
